1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,880
Can ChatGPT help you research a player
prop?

2
00:00:03,890 --> 00:00:06,870
Yes—but it should not be the source of
truth for a

3
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:10,000
current line, injury, lineup, or outcome.

4
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:13,160
Use it as a skeptical research assistant:

5
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:17,840
give it a precise question, require
sources and counterarguments,

6
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:20,900
and tell it to stop when current evidence
is incomplete.

7
00:00:22,220 --> 00:00:24,690
In this video, I’ll show you a better
prompt,

8
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:28,310
what it can and cannot do, and how to
verify the

9
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:30,220
answer before you rely on it.

10
00:00:31,020 --> 00:00:32,840
Start by making the question specific.

11
00:00:33,560 --> 00:00:35,980
“Is this player good tonight?” is too
vague.

12
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:39,740
Name the sport, player, stat, exact line,

13
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:43,630
source or platform, and whether you want
to evaluate both sides

14
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:45,560
or challenge an initial lean.

15
00:00:46,220 --> 00:00:48,140
That exact line matters.

16
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:52,030
A half point, a changed number, or a
different stat creates

17
00:00:52,040 --> 00:00:56,460
a different question. If an AI cannot
verify the current line,

18
00:00:56,740 --> 00:00:58,940
the right answer is not a confident
prediction.

19
00:00:59,860 --> 00:01:02,400
It is: stop and verify the line.

20
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:07,750
Propeller’s free AI Betting Prompt Builder
turns those details into a

21
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:10,390
research brief you can use with ChatGPT,

22
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:14,480
Claude, Gemini, or another general AI
assistant.

23
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:16,380
It is not a pick generator.

24
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:20,910
First, the prompt tells the assistant to
act as a skeptical

25
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:24,870
sports research assistant, not a betting
tipster.

26
00:01:24,880 --> 00:01:28,570
That changes the job from finding a flashy
answer to checking

27
00:01:28,580 --> 00:01:31,680
whether the evidence can support any
answer at all.

28
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:35,340
Next, it requires the current date and
time,

29
00:01:35,700 --> 00:01:38,840
plus the timestamp of every time-sensitive
source.

30
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:44,090
A response can sound detailed while
relying on yesterday’s injury report

31
00:01:44,100 --> 00:01:45,560
or an old line.

32
00:01:46,420 --> 00:01:49,350
It also requires a check of the exact
market line.

33
00:01:49,360 --> 00:01:52,300
If that cannot be verified, stop.

34
00:01:52,860 --> 00:01:56,480
A polished explanation built on the wrong
number is still wrong.

35
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:00,020
The next requirement is to check official
injury,

36
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:03,700
lineup, roster, and availability sources
first.

37
00:02:04,380 --> 00:02:08,620
General AI can summarize information, but
it can miss late news,

38
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:11,840
repeat a stale report, or cite a weak
source.

39
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:16,390
Verify current status rather than assuming
it because it appeared in

40
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:21,010
a chat response. After that, separate
recent form from the longer

41
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:26,380
sample; evaluate role and opportunity,
matchup, game environment,

42
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:31,010
and market context; then explain why each
piece of evidence applies

43
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:32,480
to this exact prop.

44
00:02:33,380 --> 00:02:37,290
Instead of asking, “Will this go over?”
you are asking the

45
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:41,220
assistant to show its work, distinguish
sourced facts from inference,

46
00:02:41,540 --> 00:02:44,320
and identify the strongest case for both
sides.

47
00:02:45,140 --> 00:02:49,800
The counterargument matters. A player may
have a strong recent trend,

48
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:52,800
but a teammate returning could change the
role.

49
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:56,520
A line might have moved after the
statistic you are reading.

50
00:02:57,140 --> 00:03:00,980
Good research makes those conflicts
visible instead of hiding them.

51
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:05,280
The prompt also requires direct links to
primary sources,

52
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:08,200
a list of missing or conflicting data,

53
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:11,260
and a clear separation between facts and
inference.

54
00:03:11,870 --> 00:03:14,800
It tells the assistant not to invent a
statistic,

55
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:19,560
injury, price, or citation; not to
recommend a stake;

56
00:03:20,020 --> 00:03:23,180
and not to claim a probability without
calibration evidence.

57
00:03:24,020 --> 00:03:26,720
Finally, it must end with one of three
conclusions:

58
00:03:27,820 --> 00:03:31,260
evidence leans over, evidence leans under,
or no action.

59
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:34,110
“No action” is not a failed answer.

60
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:36,860
It is the correct answer when the line,

61
00:03:36,880 --> 00:03:39,880
source, lineup, or current evidence is
incomplete.

62
00:03:41,140 --> 00:03:44,490
Here is the limit to remember: a prompt
cannot make stale

63
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:48,110
data current. It can make an AI ask better
questions,

64
00:03:48,120 --> 00:03:50,740
but you still need to verify the player,

65
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:54,400
line, source timestamps, and current
context yourself.

66
00:03:55,340 --> 00:03:57,650
That is where a product workflow matters.

67
00:03:57,660 --> 00:04:01,020
In Propeller, start with the exact player,

68
00:04:01,340 --> 00:04:04,220
stat, displayed direction, and current
line.

69
00:04:04,780 --> 00:04:09,220
Then inspect the sport-specific signals
that support or challenge the analysis.

70
00:04:10,060 --> 00:04:14,570
The agent breakdown makes agreement and
conflict visible rather than burying

71
00:04:14,580 --> 00:04:16,060
them in a single answer.

72
00:04:17,080 --> 00:04:19,300
When you see confidence, read it
correctly.

73
00:04:19,860 --> 00:04:25,310
Propeller’s 50-to-100 confidence score
describes how strongly the available
signals

74
00:04:25,320 --> 00:04:28,000
support the displayed More or Less
direction.

75
00:04:28,700 --> 00:04:31,320
It is not the exact chance the prop will
hit,

76
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:32,840
and it is not a guarantee.

77
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:36,100
Use the prompt to structure your
questions.

78
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:40,530
Use current sources and the Propeller
Analyzer to inspect the line

79
00:04:40,540 --> 00:04:44,670
and evidence. If the information has
changed or does not hold

80
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:46,740
together, pause or pass.

81
